## Inmates MUST NOT have clandestine comms
## =======================================
# Notes:
#   • chromium → libcups → libavahi-client & -common (src:avahi)
#   • pipewire-audio → libspa-0.2-bluetooth → libbluetooth (src:bluez)
#     FIXME: if we install wireplumber + pipewire-pulse + pipewire-alsa (not pipewire-audio),
#            I *think* all apps will continue working, and we can avoid the bluetooth dependency.
#   • It is THEORETICALLY possible to use wesnoth<->wesnoth-server and then do in-game chat,
#     which would give the inmate a clandestine comms channel.
#   • We use systemd-networkd.
#     Other network clients should be absent.
#     Inmate might use them to set up custom networking.
#   • nftables → libxtables (src:iptables)
# mmdebstrap forky /dev/null http://localhost:3142/deb.debian.org/debian --components=main,contrib,non-free,non-free-firmware --quiet --customize-hook='APT_CONFIG=$MMDEBSTRAP_APT_CONFIG HOME=$1/root '"aptitude search --disable-columns -F ' %p,' '?not(?name(-dev$)) ?or(?source-package(^.*bluetooth.*$), ?source-package(^.*bluez.*$) ?not(?reverse-depends(?reverse-depends(pipewire-audio))))' | fmt -w132"
